Compiling kmod inside /sources

1. Navigate to the sources directory and download kmod:

`cd /sources`
`curl -O https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/linux/utils/kernel/kmod/kmod-31.tar.xz`

2. Extract the archive and enter the build directory:

`tar -xf kmod-31.tar.xz`
`cd kmod-31`

3. Configure, compile, and install kmod:

`./configure --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc --bindir=/bin --with-zstd --with-xz --with-zlib`
`make -j$(nproc)`
`make install`

4. Create essential module utility symlinks back to kmod:

`ln -sf /bin/kmod /sbin/depmod`
`ln -sf /bin/kmod /sbin/insmod`
`ln -sf /bin/kmod /sbin/lsmod`
`ln -sf /bin/kmod /sbin/modinfo`
`ln -sf /bin/kmod /sbin/modprobe`
`ln -sf /bin/kmod /sbin/rmmod`

5. Clean up the build workspace:

`cd /sources`
`rm -rf kmod-31*`
